    pharm: "1. Nephroprotective therapy: Losartan 50mg daily (max tolerated dose 100mg — reduces proteinuria and slows CKD progression). Add SGLT2i: Dapagliflozin 10mg daily (slows CKD progression, reduces albuminuria, CV benefit) — when eGFR >25. 2. Optimise BP target <130/80 mmHg. 3. Stop Metformin (contraindicated when eGFR <30 — risk of lactic acidosis). Switch insulin or sulfonylurea as needed to control glucose. 4. Anaemia management: Start Darbepoetin alfa (ESA) 0.45 mcg/kg SC weekly OR Epoetin alfa 50 units/kg SC 3x/week — target Hb 10-12 g/dL. Iron: Ferrous sulphate 200mg TID or IV iron (if ferritin <100 or TSAT <20%). 5. Mineral bone disease: Calcitriol 0.25-0.5mcg daily (for secondary hyperparathyroidism). Phosphate binders: Calcium carbonate 500-1000mg with meals OR Sevelamer if hypercalcaemia. 6. Metabolic acidosis: Sodium bicarbonate 600mg TID (target bicarbonate >22). 7. Diuretics: Furosemide 40mg daily for oedema (titrate as needed). 8. Vaccinations: HBV, influenza, pneumococcal.",
    nonPharm: "Dietary: Reduce salt (<2g/day), moderate protein (0.8 g/kg/day), limit K+ (avoid oranges, bananas, potatoes, tomatoes), limit phosphate (avoid soda, processed foods, organ meats). Fluid restriction if oedema or hyponatraemia. AV fistula education and vein preservation.",
    carePlan: "Refer to nephrology for CKD management. Calculate eGFR monthly. Start Dapagliflozin 10mg if eGFR >25. Start ESA + iron. Start Calcitriol. Optimise BP and proteinuria. Educate on renal diet. Discuss RRT options: haemodialysis, peritoneal dialysis, or pre-emptive transplant. AV fistula creation when eGFR approaches 15-20.",
    dtps: "1. Advanced CKD with multiple complications requiring comprehensive nephrology care. 2. Multiple medication adjustments needed due to declining renal function (stop metformin, dose-adjust others). 3. Preparation for RRT needed in the near future.",
